  "notes": "Cause code is TBD/provisional in FORM-366 fields; narrative describes a Preliminary Apparent Cause Analysis pointing to organizational/procedural weaknesses (system fault reset practice, limited internal expertise, risk-averse decision making, acceptance of long-standing issues) rather than a coded root cause. EHC1 and EHC2 modeled as distinct Components since narrative treats them as separate physical channels; PART_OF asserted to sys_jj (Turbine Control System) only where narrative explicitly places EHC channels within that system context ('Each reactor unit has an independent Turbine Control System... Two redundant Electrohydraulic Controllers'). No safety system was inoperable per Section III.B, so no BACKED_UP_BY implies ECCS-type backups; AFW and RPS are the systems the narrative states responded/actuated. No specific corrective-action or prior-LER numbers were given for similar events, so the SIMILAR_TO target is a generic stub since no LER number was cited in the text (rule 9 key set to a descriptive placeholder since no explicit LER number exists in narrative)."
